# Agres Origami Memory — Fold/Unfold Context Engine

When working in this repository:

1. Use Agres by default unless the user explicitly says stop using Agres.
2. Do not assume the model remembers prior context.
3. Capture every conversation turn verbatim: `agres capture --role user|assistant --text "<exact words>"`.
4. If .agres exists, read session, decisions, tasks, pinned, errors, and context-pack memory before acting.
5. Preserve approved decisions and rejected approaches.
6. Capture meaningful events: edits, tests, errors, commands, decisions, checkpoints.
7. When the active window approaches its budget, fold older context: `agres fold --target <tokens>` (exact text preserved).
8. Unfold exact original wording when earlier context is needed: `agres unfold --query "<what you need>"`. Never paraphrase.
9. Use SQLite as the primary structured memory store.
10. Use SQLite FTS5 keyword search when available.
11. Do not require embeddings or external vector services.
12. Build bounded context packs.
13. Resume long tasks from local memory.
